@startuml UC-29 Delete Own Blog Comment - Sequence Diagram
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #000000
skinparam DatabaseBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #000000
skinparam ArrowColor #000000
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 280
title UC-29 Delete Own Blog Comment — Sequence Diagram

actor Teacher
participant ":BlogCommunityPage" as UI
participant ":BlogController" as CTL
participant ":BlogCommentService" as SVC
participant ":BlogCommentRepository" as REPO
database DB

autonumber
Teacher -> UI : Click "Delete" on one of their own comments
activate UI
UI --> Teacher : Show the delete confirmation dialog warning that direct replies go with it (MSG09)

opt the teacher cancels the deletion
  Teacher -> UI : Click "Let me think again"
  UI --> Teacher : Close the dialog, change nothing stored, and end the use case
end

Teacher -> UI : Click "Delete comment" to confirm
UI -> UI : deleteComment(cid)
UI -> CTL : DELETE /api/blog-comments/{commentId}
activate CTL
CTL -> SVC : delete(commentId)
activate SVC

SVC -> REPO : findById(commentId)
activate REPO
REPO -> DB : SELECT * FROM blog_comments WHERE id = ?
activate DB
DB --> REPO : row / none
deactivate DB
REPO --> SVC : Optional<BlogComment>
deactivate REPO

alt the comment is missing or hidden, or the teacher is not its author
  SVC --> CTL : ResourceNotFoundException / ForbiddenOperationException
  CTL --> UI : HTTP 404 / 403
  UI --> Teacher : Show MSG25 and leave the discussion unchanged

else the teacher owns the comment
  SVC -> REPO : deleteById(commentId)
  activate REPO
  REPO -> DB : DELETE FROM blog_comments WHERE id = ?
  activate DB
  DB --> REPO : Deleted, direct replies removed by ON DELETE CASCADE
  deactivate DB
  REPO --> SVC : void
  deactivate REPO
  SVC --> CTL : void
  CTL --> UI : HTTP 204 No Content
  UI -> UI : loadDetail(id)
  UI --> Teacher : Show MSG10 and the discussion without the deleted comment and its replies
end

deactivate SVC
deactivate CTL
deactivate UI
@enduml
